WEBVTT

00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.280
Contact Dr. Kuzumi, at Jounan 
University, immediately!

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.660
Debris has been identified as part 
of the abandoned <i>SS Tiangong</i>.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.480
It isn't responding to our attempts to access it.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.240
Current estimated point of impact

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.490
is Ulan Bator, a densely populated area.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.740
Any word from the Security Council yet?

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.190
I've made multiple attempts through 
Foreign Affairs and the Cabinet ministers,

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.370
but nothing yet!

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.050
They won't just abandon them, right?

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.880
A UN Investigation Team recovered heretical 
technology and Dr. Nastassja's body

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.100
from one of Frontier's parts

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.380
floating around the Lagrange points.

00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:37.510
And now they're having system 
trouble on their way back...

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:41.210
Approval's been granted!

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:44.850
We've been given authorization for extranational 
action, within Security Council parameters!

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:45.770
Okay!

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:49.170
Let's show those bureaucrats 
what's what... Fujitaka!

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.580
I completed the orbital calculations ages ago.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.050
Rechecking system.

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:07.210
Adjust our orbit, so we avoid landing 
on a populated area, at least.

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:09.010
I know that!

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:13.910
A missile?

00:01:13.910 --> 00:01:16.180
Are they trying to shoot us down?

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:19.430
I guess they don't have a choice.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:21.680
It's all right. Everything is just fine!

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.890
So don't give up on living!

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:31.900
<i>A song begins, a heartbeat begins.</i>

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:36.010
<i>The sound of hope fills the air.</i>

00:01:36.010 --> 00:01:39.670
<i>It says, "Don't give up on living."</i>

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:43.080
<i>And shows us the beginning 
of your passionate dream.</i>

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.000
<i>Burst, for there are no lies in this miracle!</i>

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.130
This thing's as tough to deal with as Yukine.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:57.720
Then just try and keep riding it, senpai.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:07.930
Tachibana!

00:02:07.930 --> 00:02:08.710
Right!

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:15.150
The wielders are on board. Deceleration has begun.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.000
Recalculating crash point.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.290
The ship remains on a crash course 
for the Karakorum mountains.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:23.920
Take care...

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:24.990
...of Mom.

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:28.330
<i>What do your hands exist to hold?</i>

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.290
<i>Waiting probably won't get it for you.</i>

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.500
<i>What do those hands exist to protect?</i>

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:40.510
<i>The heat you feel is the spark 
to ignite tomorrow.</i>

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:43.720
<i>Now let's pull the trigger for a new era.</i>

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.130
The shuttle isn't decelerating fast enough.

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:45.720
There's no way to avoid crashing 
into the Karakorum mountains!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.760
<i>The countdown to a legendary future.</i>

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:49.730
If we could somehow get inside, 
and just get the pilots out...

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.050
<i>You won't take flight alone.</i>

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.240
But then, Mom...

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:52.710
<i>When you overcome the past,</i>

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:52.980
...won't make it home!

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:58.470
<i>you'll see the future you must 
create blooming brightly.</i>

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:56.480
That won't happen.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:01.990
Human dignity must be given the 
same weight as human life.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.500
<i>Bonds, hearts, brought together as one.</i>

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.500
<i>The sound of hope fills the air.</i>

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.500
Dr. Nastassja protected the whole world.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.500
<i>It says, "Don't give up on believing."</i>

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:08.500
So it doesn't make sense that 
she can't come home!

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:11.600
<i>Sing! The chance is never zero!</i>

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:10.660
They really are...

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.460
...so greedy.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.330
<i>Fly! And let there be light unto this miracle!</i>

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.210
Damn it.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:15.890
It's impossible.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:18.310
It's over...

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.320
We can hear a song in a burning sky.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:24.350
Don't give up!

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.220
Collision with K2 is unavoidable!

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.480
Less than one kilometer to impact!

00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:32.480
Let's go, dummy!

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.740
Punch it!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:07.760
Adjusting K2 to the rank of Earth's 
third-highest mountain.

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.270
The shuttle is attempting a crash landing.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:20.900
<i>Open the path toward an unseen future,</i>

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.780
<i>and nothing is impossible.</i>

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.950
<i>I've never felt so strong and safe.</i>

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:30.440
<i>Always, always, always believing in one another.</i>

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.080
<i>And punching through!</i>

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:36.200
<i>Even if darkness threatens to suck me in...</i>

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.830
Go left, Tachibana!

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:39.250
<i>Even if even our blood turns to tears...</i>

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:42.420
<i>We have a place to go home to.</i>

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.960
<i>Come together! Protect! Vow!</i>

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:51.140
<i>The manifestation of our courage is a miracle.</i>

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.970
If we can just keep on like this to the base...

00:04:54.470 --> 00:04:55.310
Crap!

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.300
A village!

00:04:58.980 --> 00:04:59.750
Dummy!

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.270
What are you...

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:06.370
<i>Bonds, hearts, brought together as one.</i>

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.480
<i>The sound of hope fills the air.</i>

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:12.450
<i>It says, "Don't give up on believing."</i>

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.290
Tachibana!

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.450
Buddha, save us!

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.330
<i>Sing!</i>

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.750
<i>The chance is never zero!</i>

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.530
<i>Fly!</i>

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:20.260
<i>And let there be light unto this miracle!</i>

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.200
Mission complete.

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.180
Are you okay, Tachibana?

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:08.470
Did you get hit somewhere you shouldn't have?

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:10.600
I'm so happy

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:14.090
because of the miracle that allows 
me to use a Symphogear!

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:20.140
You really are a dummy.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:42.630
<b>UN Supernatural Disaster Response Team 
Task Force S.O.N.G.</b>

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:49.510
Here. Have something warm.

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.780
Thanks for giving me something warm.

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:52.850
That's rare.

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:54.480
You didn't need to say the last part.

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:59.810
Since the shuttle was rescued, 
it's been three months.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:01.630
After that incident,

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:05.030
Section 2 was reconstituted as S.O.N.G., 
under direct control of the UN,

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:08.570
and its primary job is now disaster 
intervention across the world.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.060
I'll be really happy

00:07:11.060 --> 00:07:13.990
if I can keep going till retirement 
without a major incident.

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.350
Unidentified signal detected 
near Yokohama Port.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:25.390
It vanished?

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.870
Contact the commander immediately!

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:28.560
Roger.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.060
<i>The legacy of Dvergr Dáinn.</i>

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.520
<i>The way I must atone is</i>

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:54.570
<i>by delivering this legacy, 
before it's all too late.</i>

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:02.680
Plain doesn't suit me...

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:04.680
So next time,

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:06.850
it'll be flashy.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.100
You do your homework?

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:17.890
Chris-chan—

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.940
I'm older than you. 
And at school, I'm your senpai!

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.360
You're setting a bad example for them.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:28.940
Good morning, Shirabe-chan and Kirika-chan.

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:31.130
Good morning...

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:32.610
Greetings!

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.040
It's hot, but you're the same as ever, huh?

00:08:38.260 --> 00:08:41.250
It's hot, but you're the same as ever, huh?

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:43.200
Oh, well... You see,

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.590
Shirabe's hands are so cold,

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:48.200
I just want to hold them.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:51.120
Kirika-chan's squishy biceps are

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.880
nice and cold, too.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:54.880
Is that true?

00:08:56.150 --> 00:08:56.760
Squish.

00:08:58.340 --> 00:09:00.510
Stop! Stop! Stop!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.060
Do that stuff at home.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:10.570
It's almost time for parent meetings 
about our post-graduation plans.

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:13.370
What a downer. I'd rather have my dad hearing

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.060
about my grades than my mom...

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:17.990
Who's coming for you, Bikky?

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.100
Ah... My grandma, maybe...

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:25.000
I don't have a dad, and my mom 
works, even on Sundays.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.980
That's pretty common.

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:28.460
I've heard every place's busy.

00:09:29.100 --> 00:09:30.030
Oh.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:31.870
Is your granny nice?

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.830
If she isn't, Bikky's grades are gonna...

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:34.570
Jump!

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:40.450
Forget that stuff, let's swim.

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:43.020
If we're taking a nap so we 
can stay up all night,

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.230
being a little tired will be good, right?

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:48.540
I said that myself, but it's an 
idea that even surprises me!

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:49.940
Okay!

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:50.980
Go!

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.490
She's only pretending she's fine, though.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:58.730
I understand...

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.890
You're spending my class napping,

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:05.000
so you can stay up all night tonight.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:08.260
That's what this is! Right, Tachibana-san?!

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.510
So, why my house?

00:10:16.510 --> 00:10:20.460
Sorry for coming over so late 
with this many people.

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:22.700
The time difference to London 
is about eight hours!

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:25.590
If we want to enjoy the charity rock festival,

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:27.310
this is the only way.

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:30.400
Well, just think of it as being a reliable senpai.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.520
And now that she can finally follow her dreams,

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.360
it's Tsubasa-san's first performance.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:37.810
Everyone's gotta cheer her on...

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:40.410
Don't we?

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.410
And one more person.

00:10:43.090 --> 00:10:44.030
Maria.

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:46.910
The songstress collaboration unit is back!

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:50.420
<b><i>Starry Sky 

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:59.510
<i>Independent at a genetic level,</i>

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:03.430
<i>holding hope and despair,</i>

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:09.730
<i>struggle until the very end!</i>

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:36.920
<i>A kiss of light and water droplets,</i>

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:42.260
<i>the birth of a rainbow like love.</i>

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:46.330
<i>Even on the most beautiful day,</i>

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.670
<i>something is born,</i>

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:51.480
<i>and something dies.</i>

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.270
<i>So at least I'll sing,</i>

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:56.110
<i>"I love you."</i>

00:11:56.110 --> 00:12:00.610
<i>Even if the world is a terrible hell...</i>

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:03.360
<i>So at least I'll share with you,</i>

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.190
<i>"I love you."</i>

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:09.780
<i>The time of liberation is upon us.</i>

00:12:09.780 --> 00:12:13.500
<i>Sing and take flight into a starry sky.</i>

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:19.470
<i>Liberty song!</i>

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:22.100
<i>Stardust!</i>

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:27.690
<i>Now shout that a miracle isn't 
something you wait for,</i>

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:31.810
<i>but something you create yourself.</i>

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:35.000
<i>Let the bitterness of the past, when you cried,</i>

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:37.060
<i>be a requiem.</i>

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:41.280
<i>And let the power of all living things</i>

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.730
<i>shine in a future world!</i>

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:44.990
<i>Believe and bring light!</i>

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:50.490
<i>Starry Sky Galaxy Cross!</i>

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:15.270
I can't believe my friends saved 
the world with those two!

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.720
It's like something out of an anime!

00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:18.860
Yeah, you're totally right...

00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:24.860
You worked hard out there tonight.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:27.190
It isn't as hard as surveillance on an idol.

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:29.480
We aren't surveillance. 
We're providing protection.

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:33.580
Many people are after the life of the 
heroine who saved the world.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:37.520
Maria was made into a scapegoat to end

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:41.520
the falling-Moon and Frontier-surfacing incidents.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:46.250
She was forced into being an idol,

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:49.360
literally a false goddess, 
to protect the adults' system.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:50.690
That isn't true.

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.930
I think what Maria-san protects is

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:59.350
an everyday life, where everyone can be happy.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:00.800
Miku...

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:03.300
That's right!

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:07.010
That's why we need to support her.

00:14:07.010 --> 00:14:07.920
Yeah!

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:25.400
A major fire has broken out in Sector 7.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:28.130
Firefighting operations are having trouble, 
and they've requested backup.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:30.600
Okay! On our way!

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:31.540
Hibiki...

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:33.470
Don't worry! We're going to save people!

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:34.780
We'll...

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:35.720
...help, too!

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.480
You guys, stay here!

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:40.380
We can't let you go out there without LiNKER!

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:57.210
Wind...

00:14:57.720 --> 00:14:58.830
Is someone there?

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.110
The tainted hero of the Frontier Incident,

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:05.960
crafted from a plea bargain and
 some cunning media manipulation,

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.210
Maria Cadenzavna Eve.

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:09.510
Who's there?

00:15:26.720 --> 00:15:27.610
Get away from him!

00:15:45.230 --> 00:15:49.200
You lack the Symphogear you should be 
wearing, so I'm uninterested in you.

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:54.190
Dance, as I will you.

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:16.800
The area is almost completely evacuated.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:21.050
But there are still multiple life 
signs in this condo block.

00:16:21.050 --> 00:16:22.410
Are people still in there?

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:25.800
It looks like they're on the 
other side of a firewall.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:27.560
What worries me more

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:30.920
is the fact that the damage keeps 
spreading toward four o'clock.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:33.470
Is some firebug going on a rampage?

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:35.620
Hibiki-kun, rescue the trapped people.

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:38.710
Chris-kun, I want you to investigate the situation.

00:16:38.710 --> 00:16:39.720
Roger!

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:52.360
No!

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:00.490
I'm counting on you.

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:02.160
I've got this!

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:10.420
<i>Balwisyall nescell Gungnir tron.</i>

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:48.570
<i>A right hand, resolved to break through,</i>

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.660
I'll guide you to the signal coordinates.

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:54.030
<i>as the sound that I am resounds.</i>

00:17:54.030 --> 00:17:59.630
<i>The courage to carry you beyond how or why,</i>

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:59.330
Do you hear something?

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:04.600
<i>clutched in an unwavering fist.</i>

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:02.970
Is this... a song?

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:05.910
<i>Be brave! Let's shout!</i>

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:10.150
<i>Just keep moving forward.</i>

00:18:07.400 --> 00:18:08.230
Tsubasa!

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.310
<i>Reach them! Let's shout!</i>

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:14.650
When my friend is in trouble, 
how could I not come to her aid?

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:15.970
<i>You're the type to give it everything you've got.</i>

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:17.120
I have been waiting for you.

00:18:15.970 --> 00:18:18.750
<i>Break through the walls, 
break through with my heart.</i>

00:18:17.420 --> 00:18:19.000
Who are you?

00:18:18.750 --> 00:18:21.190
<i>As long as there's a song in my heart,</i>

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:23.910
<i>believing in justice and clutching tight.</i>

00:18:22.340 --> 00:18:23.910
Autoscorer.

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:29.580
<i>Be a flower, blooming in your own color!</i>

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:25.870
Autoscorer?

00:18:27.050 --> 00:18:30.130
I have come to hear your song.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:32.520
<i>Don't be a hero, just be loud!</i>

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:35.230
<i>G-Beat, max out.</i>

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:37.760
<i>G-Beat, the meter.</i>

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:39.860
Hibiki-chan, destroy the wall 
ninety degrees to your left,

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:42.190
<i>I'll protect you with this song, 
and with my own hands.</i>

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.000
and make another way through.

00:18:42.190 --> 00:18:43.560
<i>Pierce through!</i>

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.930
<i>G-Beat, let your beliefs burn bright.</i>

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:48.230
<i>G-Beat, violent and clear.</i>

00:18:48.230 --> 00:18:50.900
<i>I don't need limits. I don't care about them.</i>

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:56.760
<i>I'll grab you and never let go!</i>

00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:58.370
This is the evacuation route!

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.420
Hibiki-chan, there's one final life sign.

00:19:05.520 --> 00:19:06.590
<i>Just be loud!</i>

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:09.380
<i>G-Beat, max out.</i>

00:19:09.380 --> 00:19:11.590
<i>G-Beat, the meter.</i>

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:12.350
Mommy...

00:19:11.590 --> 00:19:16.300
<i>I'll protect you with this song, 
and with my own hands.</i>

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:17.460
<i>Pierce through!</i>

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:20.090
<i>G-Beat, let your beliefs burn bright.</i>

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.260
<i>G-Beat, violent and clear.</i>

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:25.100
<i>I don't need limits. I don't care about them.</i>

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:30.940
<i>I'll grab you and never let go!</i>

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:38.190
Blades whistling in the wind...

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:40.300
Forming a circle, with wings of flame they cut.

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.070
Let the Moon shine!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:48.450
<b>Fuurin Kazan Shining Moon</b>

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:02.400
No one's found my daughter yet!

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:03.580
She hasn't been rescued—

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:04.450
Please take care of this girl!

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:05.600
Kou-chan!

00:20:05.980 --> 00:20:08.020
She's inhaled a lot of smoke.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:09.370
Kou-chan! It's okay now!

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:09.370
Get her to a hospital immediately!

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:11.110
Mommy's here!

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:11.620
Thank you for your help.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:25.130
If it is not a divine miracle,

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:28.100
it is the devil's wisdom, and too 
much for human hands!

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:29.960
Let there be a judgment!

00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:34.270
Purify the taint of Izark 
with flames that cleanse sin!

00:20:34.270 --> 00:20:36.560
Daddy! Daddy!

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:38.530
Daddy!

00:20:38.530 --> 00:20:40.640
Carol... Live,

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:42.720
and know more of the world.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:44.400
The world?

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:46.890
Carol, that is your...

00:20:51.180 --> 00:20:52.080
<i>Daddy...</i>

00:20:55.090 --> 00:20:57.440
<i>I wish that memory would just disappear.</i>

00:20:59.280 --> 00:21:01.110
It's dangerous up there!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.760
Were you separated from your mom and dad?

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:08.230
It's dangerous up there, 
so just stay put until I—

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:08.950
Silence.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:15.290
The enemy! An enemy attack!

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:16.710
What's going on there?

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.030
The enemy?

00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:26.830
That's going too far! Against another human...

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:28.770
Too far?

00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:30.750
When I fought her, I could tell.

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:34.440
She was an absolute

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:37.100
monster!

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:42.090
I'd heard your songs were far better than that...

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:46.130
Indeed, I certainly cannot let 
you beat me with that.

00:21:46.850 --> 00:21:49.950
The alchemy of Carol Malus Dienheim

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:52.080
will destroy the world

00:21:52.320 --> 00:21:55.080
and complete the Apocalypse of All Things.

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.460
Destroy the world?

00:21:58.090 --> 00:22:00.710
I am going to slay a miracle.

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:14.930
<b>Episode 1 
Murderer of Miracles</b>
